WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.650
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY
MOBILE SUIT</b>

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:25.100
EVE OF THE DECISIVE BATTLE

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.730
"Eve of the Decisive Battle".

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:38.500
If we use the microwave cannon, we can attack, right?

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:41.400
That's just an idea! At this stage,

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:44.460
there's no way we can attack Keilas Guilie!

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.100
Then we're just waiting for them to hit us!

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:48.160
There's nothing we can do!

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.360
What's that Jinn Jahannam guy thinking?!

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:54.430
He's the type who gets off on stirring things up.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:56.930
I'm sorry to interrupt, but...

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:57.860
What?!

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:02.900
Couldn't we use the Gaunland or the Reineforce as a shield?

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:05.560
Use a ship as a shield?

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.730
What kind of nonsense are you saying?!

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.560
We barely have any firepower as it is!

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.800
We'd be able to strike a serious blow!

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:14.730
We never had any chance of beating them.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:16.930
Even if we can't destroy them,

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:20.560
if we can stop their attack on the Earth,

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:23.360
then our coming here will still have been worth it.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:27.730
True, but I'd like to consider one more tactical idea.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:30.800
Right! We need another idea!

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:32.130
Oh, I know!

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:35.630
Right, rather than use the microwaves as a cannon...

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:39.730
By changing the frequency, we can induce headaches in them!

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:40.460
Right!

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:43.330
Yeah, we can do that! We can do it!

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.700
Otis?

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.500
The microwave output from the Hiland would...

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:50.700
...probably induce some nasty head and stomach aches.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:51.860
I see!

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.300
You're pretty smart, kid!

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:55.630
Well, if you'll excuse me.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:57.960
Sure thing! We'll get this set up!

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.230
Why'd you say that?!

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:03.060
How are we supposed to look for Shahkti and Suzy?!

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:06.460
If everyone's busy, we can slip out again.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:09.460
I get you! That's why you said that.

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:10.930
How'd it go?

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.500
There will be fighting again.

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:13.830
What do you mean?

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:15.560
We're going to attack them.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.830
Tomáš, there you are!

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:20.260
Could you come to the bridge right now?

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:21.460
Now what?

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:22.730
No clue.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.560
It's probably about microwaves.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.460
Microwaves? What about them?

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.960
I don't know, either.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.330
Üso knows.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:33.700
But I'm just a civilian.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:36.260
Üso isn't a soldier, either.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:42.260
How'd it go?

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.860
They said in six hours, we'll be beaming...

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:47.660
...the Hiland's microwaves at Keilas Guilie for five minutes.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.330
So, we're charging them.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:50.200
Yeah.

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:53.660
Huh? Where'd Odelo and the others get to?

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:54.730
Dunno.

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:57.430
Well, I'm going to help my dad and the others prepare.

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:58.160
Right.

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:02.060
All hands, secure normal suits! We're depressurizing the bay!

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:19.130
Odelo and Warren should stay with the girls.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:31.300
Movement at the Hiland. Probably the League Militaire!

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:33.830
Drive them out of that neutral ground!

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:43.530
You're carrying cargo! Land carefully!

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:46.600
There are three more units after you!

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:52.960
Those are regular Federation pilots, huh?

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.230
I can't stand them.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:56.800
Cony, stand by at gate number 2.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:57.600
Right.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.300
Juca Meilasch from Bagley Team is with you. Watch her.

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:01.060
Right.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:03.860
I'll be in Shrike Team's number one position.

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:08.660
Junko looks jumpy.

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:11.930
She hates the soldiers from the Gaunland.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:15.430
Then, as her chief, you need to get her in line!

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:19.960
No, Junko can't be herself unless she does this.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:24.860
She doesn't improve when you tell her to shape up, huh?

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:29.130
Yeah. I'll be flying the number three position in her combat unit.

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:32.230
There's no misunderstanding here, is there?

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:33.930
What would I misunderstand?

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:36.860
Sorry I'm late, Commander Oliver.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:42.100
Ah, Üso. Marbet, along with your Victory, will be rear guard for Junko's team.

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:42.900
Yes, sir.

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:45.660
Hey, Marbet!

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:50.830
Um... Did I interrupt something?

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:52.060
No.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:53.900
What's that?!

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:57.800
Anti-air monitors, what are you doing?!

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.530
Launch anti-missiles!

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:01.860
Increase Minovsky particle scattering to combat density!

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:02.800
Yes, sir!

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:05.260
Cony, can you and Juca get out?

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:07.800
Roger, please do.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:10.560
Miss Junko! Victory, moving out!

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:15.830
We can't use the catapult deck because the Javelins spread their cargo all over it!

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:19.260
Huh? They've blocked the deck that much?

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.000
Like I said. Let's go!

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:23.630
Um, yes, ma'am! Üso, here I go!

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:30.930
That could have been better.

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:32.500
The enemy?!

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:35.730
Listen, if I was the enemy, you'd be dead now.

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:36.830
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:40.030
In space, your senses need to be sharper than on Earth.

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:40.830
Right.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:44.460
Feel through your machine's armor and sense what's outside.

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:45.330
Yes, ma'am.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:46.000
Ahead!

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:46.600
Right!

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:54.960
2 o'clock, low!

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:55.760
2 o'clock?!

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:06.460
Miss Junko got it.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:10.360
12 o'clock, dead ahead!

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:20.700
They got me! My monitor, too?!

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:24.500
At this point, I'm just a target for the enemy!

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:26.660
If I don't move faster...!

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:30.830
I'll have the computer compensate with the auxiliary camera.

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:34.160
If there are any shells left, I'll lose the entire head!

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:36.300
Has Shrike Team come out?

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:44.230
Just hit it!

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:48.930
Nice follow, Peggie!

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.660
Because you gave me a nice, big target, Commander!

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:53.060
11 o'clock!

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:54.200
I see it!

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:56.760
Maintain 360 degree air surveillance!

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:59.300
We may have enemies coming from other directions!

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:13.160
Odelo!

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:15.730
Did they throw you off the Reineforce?

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:18.960
I heard you guys were shorthanded, so I came over!

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:22.060
I can't believe he stowed away aboard the Fishbone.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:24.800
He wants to be your knight, Sis.

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:29.060
I think we can mount a beam rifle and that clothesline pole thing here.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:31.900
Looks like your knight came along, too.

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:32.800
Oh...!

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:34.530
Figured they'd come.

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:36.360
How are the microwaves coming?

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:38.960
Dad and the others have it set up.

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:40.760
And the mobile suit battle?

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:42.930
We're pushing them back, but...

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:47.660
We have the advantage in numbers!

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:12.030
He's not dead, right?

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:14.660
You overused your beam shield,

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:17.300
so it was easy for me to slash you.

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:18.300
Nice job!

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:19.700
Yes, ma'am!

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:21.900
Thanks to your covering me, Miss Junko!

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:25.300
I'm worried about Cony on the left. Let's go assist them!

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:26.030
Right!

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:33.930
I'm okay. My image is just a little fuzzy.

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:36.100
Because they winged your head?

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:36.960
Yes, ma'am.

00:09:37.330 --> 00:09:40.700
Miss Junko, do you like Mr. Oliver?

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:43.160
Why would you ask me that?

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:45.830
Is it wrong to be curious?

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:49.400
Yes, it is! That's grownup business!

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:50.930
Look! Here they come!

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:55.200
A dummy balloon?

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:58.500
Don't worry about unimportant things and don't use your rifle!

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:00.560
It'll just let the enemy find us!

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:01.460
Yes, ma'am!

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:05.430
It's grownup business.

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:07.860
She said they're going to attack us?

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:08.660
Yes.

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:12.000
Then you and the princess should get out of here.

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:14.400
I can't go back if they're coming for us!

00:10:14.730 --> 00:10:18.400
The Contio is ready. I'll go out and meet them, as well.

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:22.800
The princess is an important person for the empire's future.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:26.560
Keilas Guilie Fleet, halt construction of the Big Cannon!

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:28.360
Prepare to counterattack!

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:31.200
Pardon...

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:34.100
Hey, come on! Isn't the milk here, yet?

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:35.800
We've been waiting for hours!

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:37.230
That girl...

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:38.700
Ask the orderly!

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:40.700
Can't you get it yourself?

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:43.830
If I leave this room, they'll get mad at me!

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:45.700
Suzy?!

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:48.660
Suzy, let's wait.

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:50.930
Karl's still all right for now.

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:57.500
Shahkti and Karl are here, too?

00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:59.060
Miss Katejina!

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:01.560
What are you doing on a military ship?

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:04.000
I could ask you the same question.

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:05.760
We're not really sure.

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:09.500
They've told me all sorts of things and given me special treatment.

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:11.100
Special treatment?

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:28.160
Leave this to us. You get some rest.

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:29.930
Thanks, Mr. Kuffu.

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:33.230
A detached squad seems like an odd choice to make.

00:11:33.260 --> 00:11:34.260
But...

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:37.500
It feels wrong for you to give me any special treatment.

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:41.460
If you're going to say that, then I'll be truthful.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:44.960
I'm worried because Junko seems to be in a hurry to die.

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:48.260
Someone as confident as her would never do that.

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:50.000
In a hurry to die?

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:55.830
I'm afraid you'll act like her, and I want Junko to live.

00:11:56.130 --> 00:12:00.430
For that reason, you can't be at Junko's side.

00:12:01.230 --> 00:12:02.830
In that case, it's all right.

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:07.100
You are not well! Body temperature, dropping.

00:12:07.130 --> 00:12:08.830
I shall administer adrenaline!

00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:10.430
Shut up!

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:12.600
I wonder if Shahkti's alright.

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:13.600
Shahkti!

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:24.600
Any images of Miss Junko?

00:12:24.630 --> 00:12:26.400
Junko! Junko!

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:30.160
Haro, what are you doing, hiding in here?

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:32.830
Stop that! That's creepy!

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:36.460
We need to save the commander from his own carelessness.

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:39.830
So much has happened since I first met Shrike Team.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:12:59.460
Miss Junko?

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:03.030
Kid? What's up?

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:05.930
Miss Junko, don't die.

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:08.200
What's with you?

00:13:08.230 --> 00:13:11.060
Nothing. Just, please, don't get killed.

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:17.230
Who's going to get killed?

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:18.460
It's just...

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:22.800
You're great in combat, but you're too reckless.

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:25.630
You only say that because you're a newbie.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:27.930
I'm an amateur, huh?

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:28.700
Hm?

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:31.130
You should just worry about yourself.

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:32.560
Cony...

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:37.400
Huh? Where's Elisha? Isn't she coming?

00:13:37.430 --> 00:13:40.300
Tomáš and Karel are more than enough.

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:45.000
I bet you're happy because Martina's coming!

00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:47.600
Yeah. She's a feisty lady.

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:49.030
Elisha!

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:52.660
We'll go out ahead of you on a course back to our home colony.

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:56.500
Come and fight with me in the League Militaire!

00:13:56.530 --> 00:13:58.230
Martina, are you okay with this?

00:13:58.260 --> 00:14:01.960
Once we see you off, I'll come back in the Aeneas.

00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:20.530
Once everyone's off the Gaunland, it's time to charge the enemy, right?

00:14:20.730 --> 00:14:22.460
Captain Gomez! Agh!

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:23.630
Oh, sorry.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.330
Test the remote control on the Gaunland!

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:29.130
All hands, clear the tail nozzle!

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:30.860
Otis, we're ready.

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:32.500
Now, then...

00:14:32.560 --> 00:14:35.400
Try raising the output by 1%.

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:43.160
Yes! That wired control looks like it's working!

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:45.560
Mobile suit forces, prepare to launch!

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:51.030
We've added the overhang pack, but don't count on it too much.

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:52.160
Roger that!

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:53.960
Thank you.

00:15:24.130 --> 00:15:27.230
What's this pain I feel?

00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:29.760
S-Shahkti, do you hurt, too?

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:31.900
Yes.

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:36.330
What should I do? Karl is suffering so much.

00:15:36.600 --> 00:15:39.730
If he vomits, don't let him choke on it.

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:44.160
Hey, why's my stomach suddenly hurt...?

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:45.600
Again?

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:53.130
Okay, first formation!

00:15:53.330 --> 00:15:55.960
Time for the Bagley Team survivors to clear their names!

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:12.330
Miss Marbet, are you okay?

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:13.660
Something wrong?

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:16.600
No, I meant are you doing okay with that Zoloat?

00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:21.560
I'm used to it. Anti-ship combat can turn into a free-for-all,

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:23.330
so it might come in handy.

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:26.030
Maybe she's feeling better.

00:16:26.060 --> 00:16:29.130
Victory, you're clear in front. Use the catapult!

00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:31.830
Just let the catapult do the work!

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:33.060
Ready for this?

00:16:33.100 --> 00:16:33.730
Yes, sir!

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:34.230
Okay!

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:36.930
Üso Ewin, here I go! Go ahead!

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:56.900
Why are our mobile suits taking so long to deploy?

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.200
It's no use!

00:16:58.300 --> 00:17:02.100
Most of the pilots are knocked out with diarrhea and stomachaches!

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:04.560
This must be our superiors' fault!

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:05.830
Hurry up in there!

00:17:05.860 --> 00:17:07.330
Use the toilet in your own room!

00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:08.330
I wouldn't make it in time!

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:10.130
We're on Alert 1 status!

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:11.330
We need the toilet!

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:13.230
Take some spare toilet packs!

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:15.100
No way!

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:18.200
Damn the League Militaire! Using dirty tricks like this!

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:21.560
It must be microwaves!

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:25.660
We've entered the microwave territory.

00:17:25.700 --> 00:17:29.230
They'll cut the microwaves in 30 seconds. Peggie!

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:33.600
When the headaches stop, I want to wipe out some enemy ships!

00:17:34.060 --> 00:17:36.660
Üso, it's time for the preemptive strike.

00:17:39.500 --> 00:17:42.030
Shahkti might be drifting out here.

00:17:42.900 --> 00:17:45.600
As the one who suggested this, I give the signal.

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:47.960
Shahkti, please don't get hit!

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:15.860
Ship number 13, hit!

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:18.100
Three patrol ships, lost!

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:21.360
If I can assemble Keilas Guilie's Big Cannon,

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:24.660
credit for conquering Earth will be mine!

00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:26.500
It will be Zanscare's...

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:27.600
Incoming?!

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:30.330
It's not just mobile suits! Incoming ship fire, as well!

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:35.100
The microwave emission has stopped.

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:37.260
Once we engage the mobile suits,

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:39.960
open a path for the Gaunland and the Reineforce!

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:59.960
A Bagley Team EZ! There?!

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:11.030
Newbies shouldn't pretend to be regular forces!

00:19:15.030 --> 00:19:16.560
Looks like it's working.

00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:22.360
Good, good! Mr. Romero, Mr. Otis, how are the Gaunland's controls?

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:24.260
Well, Otis?

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:27.960
No problems. We even have control of the anti-air cannons.

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:38.400
Hey, is maintenance on the Contio finished yet?

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:41.100
I'm sorry, sir! Just a little longer!

00:19:41.630 --> 00:19:44.430
They have over ten Gundam-types out there?!

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:45.760
They're not "Gundams"!

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:49.430
They're Victory-types! Don't call them by that name!

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:55.130
You think Üso's coming, too?

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:58.830
Maybe. This fight now is between armies.

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:02.460
The Victory is coming.

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:04.060
You know?

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:07.930
You mean, because they've sent out all their mobile suits?

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:10.030
No...

00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:13.760
I can see the Gundam, but not Üso.

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:16.100
What do you mean?

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:18.460
I feel it.

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:26.530
Where? Where do I aim?

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:28.500
Where?!

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:42.260
Who...

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:44.060
Just this once.

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:48.930
Didn't Sis teach you? In space, your senses need to be sharper!

00:20:48.960 --> 00:20:50.160
R-Right!

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:52.630
Miss Junko, Miss Marbet...

00:20:53.300 --> 00:20:55.300
Junko! Don't be reckless!

00:20:58.360 --> 00:20:59.830
She's going to kill herself!

00:21:01.630 --> 00:21:03.200
A Zoloat web?!

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:07.930
Just a bluff!

00:21:15.560 --> 00:21:18.200
Don't be hasty! You're going in too deep, Junko!

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:19.300
Roger!

00:21:19.600 --> 00:21:21.830
Wouldn't want to worry the kid, right?

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:23.100
Exactly!

00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:28.260
All you do now is continue to clean up after Junko!

00:21:32.230 --> 00:21:33.260
Enough!

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:39.660
If she's in such a hurry to die, then let her, Oliver!

00:21:43.130 --> 00:21:44.400
Another dummy?

00:21:45.060 --> 00:21:47.600
How could I have fallen for that twice?!

00:21:56.030 --> 00:21:57.260
He's dead...

00:21:58.030 --> 00:22:01.000
Anyone who gets hit out here is sure to die!

00:23:33.930 --> 00:23:37.760
The Reineforce begins its charge on Keilas Guilie.

00:23:38.700 --> 00:23:41.000
In the swirl of flashing lights,

00:23:41.030 --> 00:23:45.830
Üso witnesses both cruelty by those who wield their weapons,

00:23:46.160 --> 00:23:48.660
and an act of kindness.

00:23:49.860 --> 00:23:52.860
Next time, on Mobile Suit Victory Gundam:

00:23:54.400 --> 00:23:55.960
Next Episode STRIKE THE STRATEGIC SATELLITE

00:23:55.960 --> 00:23:57.360
Please watch it!

00:23:57.360 --> 00:23:59.360
Next Episode STRIKE THE STRATEGIC SATELLITE
